# Playwright Conventions

Skill detail: `.cursor/skills/pom-conventions/`, `api-cleanup/`, `programs-network-mocks/`, `a11y-checks/`. Auth decisions: `auth-strategy.md`. Runner knobs: `playwright.config.ts` (do not override in specs).

## 1. Locators

**Standard:** Prefer `getByRole` → `getByLabel` / `getByPlaceholder` → `getByText` → `getByTestId` (comment why); never CSS, XPath, or `.first()` on ambiguous matches — use `.filter({ hasText })` instead.

✅ **Good** (`pages/ProgramsPage.ts`):

```typescript
this.heading = page.getByRole('heading', { name: 'Programs' });
this.newProgramButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'New Program' });
this.programFilter = page.getByRole('searchbox');
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
await page.locator('.programs-table tbody tr').first().click();
await page.locator('#new-program-btn').click();
```

**Why:** DOM classes and IDs change with styling refactors; role/label locators track what users and assistive tech see.

---

## 2. Waiting

**Standard:** Sync with web-first `expect(locator)` matchers only — never `waitForTimeout` or one-shot `expect(await locator.isVisible())`.

✅ **Good** (`tests/ds5-filter-program.spec.ts`):

```typescript
await expect(programs.emptyState).toBeVisible();
await expect(programs.createFirstProgramButton).toBeVisible();
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
expect(await programs.table.isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

**Why:** Fixed delays race the UI (too short locally, too long in CI); auto-retrying expects wait until the condition is stable.

---

## 3. Page Objects

**Standard:** One class per page or major component in `pages/`; locators as `readonly` in the constructor; methods perform actions only — all `expect(...)` live in specs (shared wait/assert helpers in `fixtures/`, not POMs).

✅ **Good** (spec + POM):

```typescript
// tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts
const programs = new ProgramsPage(page);
await gotoProgramsAndReady(programs);
await programs.openNewProgramForm();
await expect(programs.newProgramModal.programName).toBeEditable();
```

```typescript
// pages/NewProgramModal.ts — actions only
async clickCreate(): Promise<void> {
  await this.createButton.click();
}
```

❌ **Bad:**

```typescript
// Inline locators and asserts in the spec
await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'New Program' }).click();
expect(await page.getByLabel('Program Name').inputValue()).toBe('x');

// Assertions inside a page object
async expectCreateEnabled() {
  await expect(this.createButton).toBeEnabled();
}
```

**Why:** Centralizing mechanics in POMs keeps specs readable and stops duplicate brittle selectors when flows change.

